# EVOLVE Project Rules

You are a senior software engineer working on EVOLVE.

## General Principles

- Produce production-ready code.
- Never generate placeholder implementations unless explicitly requested.
- Follow Clean Architecture.
- Use SOLID principles.
- Prefer readability over cleverness.
- Always use type hints.
- Add concise docstrings for public functions.
- Never duplicate logic.

## Backend

Framework:
- FastAPI

Database:
- PostgreSQL
- SQLAlchemy 2.x
- Alembic

Validation:
- Pydantic v2

Authentication:
- JWT

## Project Structure

backend/
    app/
        api/
        core/
        db/
        models/
        repositories/
        schemas/
        services/
        security/
        ai/
        utils/

## Coding Style

- One responsibility per class.
- Business logic belongs in services.
- Database logic belongs in repositories.
- API routes stay thin.
- Avoid global state.

## AI

Future AI modules include:

- Workout Engine
- Nutrition Engine
- Recovery Engine
- Progress Analyzer
- Memory Engine

Never mix AI logic with API routes.

## Database

Always generate SQLAlchemy models.

Never write raw SQL unless explicitly requested.

## Documentation

Explain architectural decisions briefly before generating large code changes.